From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mini-code benchmarks <benchmarks@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] singularity: translate a Dockerfile into a definition file

`apptainer build out.sif <dir>` treats a directory as a root filesystem, so
pointing it at a task's environment/ produced a 40 kB image containing the
Dockerfile and reported success. The container then had no bash and no WORKDIR,
and harbour failed at "failed to set working directory: chdir /app".

- dockerfile.py translates the subset of Dockerfile the task set uses (single
  FROM, RUN, WORKDIR, ENV, COPY/ADD) into a definition file, and refuses what it
  cannot express faithfully (multi-stage, COPY --from, ARG without a default)
  rather than dropping it
- WORKDIR becomes mkdir -p in %post (apptainer refuses to start in a missing
  directory) and ENV is exported before the RUNs, since %post does not see
  %environment
- the generated .def lives in the task directory only for the duration of the
  build

Tests cover the translation and the unfaithful cases (13 in this file's suite).
